{
  "comment": [
    "Recipes are date-free. 'contains' lists allergen/dietary groups the SafetyFilter screens",
    "against constraints.hard (see Products/FamilyHub/config/policy.json).",
    "",
    "v7.2 — WHY THERE IS RED MEAT IN HERE ON PURPOSE. The household's standing preference is",
    "prefer_white_meat / chicken_turkey_fish_over_red_meat. A preference with nothing to turn",
    "down is invisible: through v7 every recipe was vegetarian, so 'prefers white meat' could",
    "not shape a single dinner, and the planner's considered/rejected line had nothing real to",
    "put in it. rcp-009 and rcp-010 exist to BE rejected — a soft preference doing visible",
    "work, which is the difference between a chip that decorates and a chip that decides.",
    "",
    "Note the two kinds of 'no'. Red meat loses to a PREFERENCE — the planner weighs it and",
    "explains itself. Pork would lose to a hard RULE and never reach the model at all (the",
    "result_screen rule drops it upstream). Both are in the demo, and they are not the same",
    "act: one is judgement, the other is a gate.",
    "",
    "Tags are a closed vocabulary — FindRecipes reports it back as 'available_tags', so a",
    "planner asking for a word that is not here is told so rather than left to guess. Keep new",
    "tags consistent with the ones already in use (more_protein, never high_protein)."
  ],
